  "answer": "\\sin z = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^n}{(2n+1)!} z^{2n+1}",
  "explanation": "The proposed solution is correct. Since \\(\\sin z\\) is an entire function, it is analytic at \\(z=0\\). Therefore, its Laurent series expansion contains no principal part (no negative powers of \\(z\\)) and coincides with its Taylor (Maclaurin) series. The derivation of coefficients and the final summation formula are accurate."
